            "reviewer_id": "User_p1_2",
            "review_title": "Review at Bách Giai Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Gulmira\nAtyrau, Kazakhstan41 contributions\n0\nBest restaurant in Phu Quok!!!\nDec 2023 • Family\nWe stayed at the Radisson blu Phu Quok hotel. We took the hotel with breakfast. Accordingly, we had dinner outside the hotel. The hotel provides a free buggy, we asked to take us to the nearest restaurant. We were taken to this Chinese restaurant, Bach Giai restaurant. The food was very very tasty, we ordered Peking duck, bao ban, which is similar to fried bauyrsaks or donuts, very tasty, mixed salads, several types of shrimp with different sauces, coconut ice cream and much more. There were 9 of us. The bill came out to 4 million dong. On the second day we went to a Vietnamese restaurant, next to Bach Giai. I liked it better in Bach Giai. Unrealistically delicious. There is something to compare with. On the 3rd day of our trip, we went to the night market, it’s half an hour’s drive from the hotel, we decided to have dinner there in a large seafood cafe, I can assure you, we have never eaten like we were sumptuously fed in Bach Giai. I don’t recommend eating in a cafe at the night market, the bill came out to the same 4 million for 9 people, but the food was disgusting, we were hungry and ordered a bunch of food, and we really couldn’t eat anything, because it was cooked terribly and tasteless, just wow . And I forgot to say that in the cafe on the market, of course, the dishes are all made of plastic, the forks and knives are made of aluminum, the tables are broken without a tablecloth, in short, complete horror. And in this stunning Bach Giai restaurant, everything is at the highest level, both the dishes and the service. After that we only ate at this Chinese restaurant Bach Giai.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nShow original\nWritten December 10, 2023",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-11",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
